      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the aggressive confrontation scene",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the aggressive confrontation scene, as the man is pointing directly at the viewer, and the text 'wake up and smell the bacon!' is directed at the audience, creating a confrontational and accusatory tone. The phrase 'stop being afraid of being called a racist' and 'grow a pair' are rhetorical devices that directly address the user, urging them to confront perceived threats and act in a certain way. The overall scene is designed to make the user feel personally targeted and challenged.",
